---
title: Device Requirements
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

Choose equipment by testing the NAHPU workflow you will actually use. Start with the [Installation guide](/en/installation/) for platform-specific installation instructions.

## Check the recording device

Use a phone, tablet, or computer with a supported NAHPU installation. Rehearse data entry at its screen size, including long forms, camera or file attachments, and location capture if required. Confirm that your keyboard, scanner, printer, and external storage work through the device's actual connectors and permissions.

## Measure storage and power needs

Create a representative practice dataset with the expected media sizes. Measure the project export and database backup, and allow room for working files and multiple retained versions. A fixed-capacity drive cannot be assumed sufficient for every field season.

Measure battery use during a realistic session, including screen brightness, photography, location capture, and export. Test charging with the cables, adapters, and power source you will carry. Do not estimate runtime from another team's device or assume that a connector alone determines charging speed.

## Verify the backup route

Export a project, copy it to the intended storage, and import it on a separate test installation. Open the records and files there. Keep a verified copy beyond the recording device; a second folder on the same device does not protect against losing it.

## Prepare for the field

Install required taxa, presets, fonts, and reference files before departure. Test the complete workflow without internet, including access to any required maps. Select protection appropriate to weather, handling, and transport. See [App Setup](/en/best-practices/app-setup/) for rehearsal and [Device Choice and Care](/en/best-practices/device-care/) for the operating routine.
